zes are mostly identical, with some of the blocks from Rally-X changed into roads to reduce dead ends, and some different flag (and rock) locations. This title was manufactured in greater numbers and was much more popular in Japan than its predecessor.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}, {"id": 38, "name": "Open world"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/new-rally-x", "videos": [{"id": 23933, "name": "Gameplay video", "video_id": "4kyuiw4fkxk", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kyuiw4fkxk", "title": "New Rally X - Namco Arcade Game 1981 (1080p)", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4kyuiw4fkxk/maxresdefault.jpg"}, {"id": 187961, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "53QdrHZxhiY", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=53QdrHZxhiY", "title": "[FM-7] New Rally-X \u30e9\u30ea\u30fcX, Fujitsu FM-7, 1984.", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/53QdrHZxhiY/maxresdefault.jpg"}], "collections": [{"id": 2121, "name": "Rally-X"}]}